id: E14849-draft-2501_91199785
trigger_tool: libusb|autotools|check
phase: runtime|testing
error_signature: "libusb_init() returned LIBUSB_ERROR_IO|sr_init() failed: -1"
severity: 2
category: optional-backend|usb|upstream-test
match_keywords: libusb_init, absent usbfs, optional backend, configure without-libusb, global initialization, complete upstream suite
title: An unavailable optional USB backend can fail a library's global initialization and all unrelated tests
root_cause: >
  Signing must be idempotent on the task-owned build copy: inspect existing ELF sections, remove an old .codesign only from that disposable copy, sign the copy, require a resulting .codesign, and atomically replace the owned original only after success. Restore the process umask and clean siblings on failure.
  A consumer launched by upstream make check needs the uninstalled producer shared-library directory, not only published dependency directories. Add the own build .libs provider to the exact subprocess environment and sign own real shared ELFs before running the unchanged registered tests.
  Some multiprotocol libraries initialize optional USB support in the global
  context constructor. When the target has no accessible USB bus, libusb_init
  fails and the entire constructor returns failure; tests for XML, transforms
  and demo drivers then fail before reaching their own assertions. Merely
  relaxing the consumer's expected return value does not restore those APIs.
affected_scope: Multiprotocol libraries whose global initializer eagerly starts an optional hardware backend
verification_cmd: "confirm the target USB capability and the upstream configure switch; disable only the unavailable backend, then run the unchanged full upstream suite and installed consumer"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: explicitly-configure-out-unavailable-optional-backend
rec_description: >
  Signing must be idempotent on the task-owned build copy: inspect existing ELF sections, remove an old .codesign only from that disposable copy, sign the copy, require a resulting .codesign, and atomically replace the owned original only after success. Restore the process umask and clean siblings on failure.
  A consumer launched by upstream make check needs the uninstalled producer shared-library directory, not only published dependency directories. Add the own build .libs provider to the exact subprocess environment and sign own real shared ELFs before running the unchanged registered tests.
  If the hardware backend is optional and the target lacks its device bus,
  use the upstream disable switch and remove the unneeded dependency. Keep
  all remaining test cases and record the feature loss. Do not stub out the
  initializer, report USB functionality, or turn failing tests into skips.
rec_auto_fix: false
forbid_1_pattern: "treat libusb initialization failure as success while exposing working USB drivers"
forbid_1_reason: this hides an unavailable hardware path and misrepresents supported functionality
similar_to: E581-draft-9B31, E548-draft-EADD
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E14849-draft-2501_91199785.md
source_event: libsigrok/0.5.2 historical optional USB backend failure; CI80119 config.status permission denied; libsigrok-w3-20261010T105000Z full76/76 consumer1/1 ConanRC0 raw log SHA256 7580a82df2b5d6bc8fe8b902a4fcf87732dbf0a248335868534e486d15ff25fe 2026-10-13 current CI repair; libsigrok-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r2, official CI log SHA256 0d9c940608577e4d33601684beeab98a5e644d2e48c5037e78c3f9b22117862d; The increment separates the build-tree producer SONAME from dependency cache providers and installed test_package runtime paths. Dependency .la overlays alone cannot provide the uninstalled producer; keep all registered checks, never make loader failures skips. 2026-10-14 current CI repair; libsigrok-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r101, official CI log SHA256 5bad284736bfa29acc7a734fe365c6fd407e8b5a332f23a2798c5599b1c8a036; Worker signer failures must retain the actual bounded stdout/stderr; a bare CalledProcessError cannot distinguish old-signature rejection from tool policy or permissions. No unsigned execution, dependency-cache rewriting, or test skips are acceptable. Current native tests prove recipe behavior, not the worker signing-policy cause.
last_updated: 2026-10-14
test_diagnostic_increment: Automake FAIL tests/main without main.log cannot identify a failed assertion or loader. On OHOS bind generated configure helpers and registered makecheck to the public system shell; publish both main.log and test-suite.log on nonzero exit, preserving every failure and76-case denominator. Shell-init/getcwd is only an error signature, not proof of the sole root cause.
ci_increment: Configuring out an unavailable optional backend does not fix generated script filesystem failures. HMDFS requires the config.status temporary directory to be created accessibly; mktemp forces0700 independently of outerumask. Strict release anchors repair both primary/fallback with exclusive taskTMPDIR mkdir underumask007 and retain all cleanup/errors and76 Checkcases.
draft: true
contributor_id: 2501_91199785
